/-
# Shimura 2004: further results

Root import for `QuadFormsKB/Literature/Shimura2004/Wave3/` (G. Shimura, *Arithmetic and Analytic Theories of
Quadratic Forms and Clifford Groups*, American Mathematical Society, 2004).

* `Lemma15`: Lemma 1.5 (ii): SO^φ(V) is transitive on nonzero vectors of a given value (n > 1, resp. n > 2).
* `Splitting`: (3.13)–(3.15) first part: A(V) = A(W) ⊕ κA(W), A^±(V) = A^±(W) ⊕ κA^∓(W), A⁺(W) = {aκ = κa}.
* `SubspaceGroup`: (3.15) second part: G^±(W) = A(W) ∩ G^±(V).
* `Lemma313`: Lemma 3.13 (both directions, with the norms); converse of (3.14).
* `CenterGroup`: Theorem 3.6 (ii), last clause: 𝔠⁺ ∩ G⁺(V) = F^× ∪ F^×z (n > 2 even), (𝔠⁺)^× (n = 2).
* `Formula320`: (3.20a,b), the stabilizer of the line Fh in G⁺(V).
* `MassSolutions`: (13.14), (13.16): mass of Λ[q,𝔟] equals #Λ[q,𝔟] in the definite case.
* `Formula1318`: Theorem 11.6 (i), (ii) stated as a named input; (13.18) proved from it.
* `RealSpin`: Theorem 14.2 (ii), algebraic part (G⁰/ℝ^× ≅ G¹/{±1} ≅ τ(G¹)); the identity-component part stated.
* `MaximalCompact`: Theorem 14.2 (iv) stated; G¹(X) ∩ G¹(Y) = {±1} proved.
* `TubeDomain`: (15.2), (15.4a), Lemma 15.4 (vector form) stated.
* `Iwasawa`: Theorem 14.3 stated (G¹ = P¹K, G⁺ = P⁺K, G⁰ = (P⁺ ∩ G⁰)K); its definiteness part proved.
-/
